  "query_preview": "..\n\nA cold front associated with a surface low in south- central \nCanada has moved through Northeast Montana this morning. Strong \nnorthwest flow aloft and a tight pressure gradient is\nstrengthening winds out of the northwest through this evening\nbefore becoming light and variable tonight. A Lake Wind Advisory \nremains in effect until 5 PM MDT.\n\nThe upper-level trough will rapidly exit eastward overnight into\nFriday morning ahead of a strong upper- level ridge over the \nwestern United States. As a result, warm and dry conditions are \nexpected this weekend. Minor embedded disturbances aloft may \nslightly enhance southwest winds, but no significant deviations \nfrom the ridge- induced weather regime are expected. \n\nBeyond a dry frontal passage this weekend, warmer and drier\nconditions should persist through early next week. Meanwhile, an\nupper low off of the west coast will dig south into central\nCalifornia mid-week. Current model guidance is keeping Northwest \nMontana relatively dry during this period, and little change to \nforecast QPF is anticipated.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n\n- There is high confidence in conditions remaining largely benign\n  throughout the forecast period\n\n- No deviations from the NBM\n\nKENZ",
